    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67002" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταυδάω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speak among</i>, and so <i>address</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always c. dat. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθανάτοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπεα Τρώεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.496
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπε᾽ Ἀργείοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.109
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				18.139
			</span></i>, al., and always in 3sg.
			impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετηύδα</span>, exc.
				1sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετηύδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.153
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				270
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖον ἔπος πάντεσσι μετηύδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.773
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later c. acc.
			pers., <i>accost, address</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				4.61
			</span></i>.</div>
